<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="wrap">

  <div class="af-hero">
    <div class="af-hero-copy">
      <span class="af-kicker">Free Chrome extension</span>
      <h1>₹1 deals don't wait for you to finish typing 🏃</h1>
      <p class="af-lede">By the time you've picked the address, scrolled to Net Banking, found your bank and hit Place Order, the good stuff is gone. <b>AmaFast does all of that the moment you click Buy&nbsp;Now.</b></p>
      <div class="af-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary btn-lg" href="<%= release.download %>" download>⬇ Download AmaFast v<%= release.version %></a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="#install">How to install →</a>
      </div>
      <p class="af-meta">Free forever · Chrome <%= release.minChrome %>+ · Amazon.in · 40&nbsp;KB · no account, no tracking</p>
    </div>
    <div class="af-hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="af-clock">
        <div class="af-clock-ring"></div>
        <div class="af-clock-face"><b>0:04</b><span>gone</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% if (showcase && showcase.length) { %>
    <div class="af-showcase">
      <h2>Deals that disappear in a blink</h2>
      <p class="af-sub">Live on IndiaOffers right now. These are exactly the ones you lose by checking out slowly.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <% showcase.forEach(function (d, i) { %>
          <%- include('partials/deal-card', { d: d, storeMap: storeMap, eager: i < 2 }) %>
        <% }); %>
      </div>
      <p class="af-showcase-foot"><a class="btn-ghost" href="/loot-deals">See all loot deals →</a></p>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What it actually does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Skips the clicking.</b> Address, delivery speed, Internet Banking, your bank — the steps you'd do by hand while stock runs out.</li>
      <li><b>Puts our deals in your toolbar.</b> Today's loot deals with live prices, one click to open.</li>
      <li><b>Flags a deal on the product page.</b> On a product we track, AmaFast shows the price we have on record for it.</li>
      <li><b>Leaves the paying to you.</b> It stops at the bank page and opens Your Orders, where you pay with UPI, a card, or whatever you like.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="af-install" id="install">
    <h2>Install it in 4 steps ⚙️</h2>
    <p class="af-sub">AmaFast is <b>not on the Chrome Web Store</b> — it needs a permission the store doesn't hand out easily, so you install it yourself. One minute, once.</p>

    <ol class="af-stepgrid">
      <li>
        <div class="af-stepnum">1</div>
        <div class="af-stepbody">
          <h3>Download and unzip</h3>
          <p>You'll get a folder called <code>amafast</code>. Put it somewhere permanent — Documents is fine. <b>If you delete this folder the extension stops working.</b></p>
          <a class="btn-primary" href="<%= release.download %>" download>⬇ Download v<%= release.version %></a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li>
        <div class="af-stepnum">2</div>
        <div class="af-stepbody">
          <h3>Open Chrome's extensions page</h3>
          <p>Chrome blocks websites from opening this page for you — a security rule, nothing we can change. So copy the address and paste it into your address bar:</p>
          <div class="af-copy">
            <code id="af-url">chrome://extensions</code>
            <button type="button" class="btn-primary" id="af-copy-btn" data-copy="chrome://extensions">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <p class="af-tiny">Paste it in the address bar and press Enter.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li>
        <div class="af-stepnum">3</div>
        <div class="af-stepbody">
          <h3>Turn on Developer mode</h3>
          <p>Top-right of that page. Flip it on and a new row of buttons appears.</p>
          <svg class="af-ui" viewBox="0 0 320 84" role="img" aria-label="Developer mode toggle at the top right of the extensions page">
            <rect x="1" y="1" width="318" height="82" rx="8" fill="var(--af-ui-bg)" stroke="var(--af-ui-line)"/>
            <text x="16" y="28" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="var(--af-ui-ink)">Extensions</text>
            <text x="196" y="28" font-size="11" fill="var(--af-ui-muted)">Developer mode</text>
            <rect x="282" y="17" width="26" height="14" rx="7" fill="#0f6e56"/>
            <circle cx="301" cy="24" r="5" fill="#fff"/>
            <rect x="16" y="48" width="86" height="22" rx="6" fill="var(--af-ui-accent)"/>
            <text x="27" y="63" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">Load unpacked</text>
            <rect x="110" y="48" width="64" height="22" rx="6" fill="var(--af-ui-chip)"/>
            <text x="124" y="63" font-size="11" fill="var(--af-ui-muted)">Pack</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li>
        <div class="af-stepnum">4</div>
        <div class="af-stepbody">
          <h3>Click "Load unpacked" and pick the folder</h3>
          <p>Choose the <code>amafast</code> folder itself — the one with <code>manifest.json</code> inside. <b>Not</b> the <code>src</code> folder inside it.</p>
          <svg class="af-ui" viewBox="0 0 320 96" role="img" aria-label="Choose the amafast folder, not the src folder inside it">
            <rect x="1" y="1" width="318" height="94" rx="8" fill="var(--af-ui-bg)" stroke="var(--af-ui-line)"/>
            <text x="16" y="24" font-size="11" fill="var(--af-ui-muted)">Select the extension directory</text>
            <rect x="12" y="32" width="296" height="24" rx="6" fill="rgba(15,110,86,.12)" stroke="#0f6e56"/>
            <text x="24" y="48" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="var(--af-ui-ink)">📁 amafast</text>
            <text x="250" y="48" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#0f6e56">← this one</text>
            <text x="40" y="72" font-size="12" fill="var(--af-ui-muted)">📁 src</text>
            <text x="250" y="72" font-size="11" fill="var(--af-ui-muted)">✕ not this</text>
            <text x="40" y="88" font-size="12" fill="var(--af-ui-muted)">📄 manifest.json</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="af-note"><b>Chrome will warn you — that's normal.</b> Every time you restart Chrome you'll see a bubble asking you to disable developer-mode extensions. Click <b>Keep</b> or just close it. That appears for every extension installed this way, not just ours.</p>
    <p class="af-note af-note-good"><b>It starts in Test mode on purpose.</b> On your first checkout it does everything up to choosing your bank, then <b>stops without placing the order</b> — so you can watch exactly what it does before trusting it with real money. Turn Test mode off in Settings when you're happy.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>Because it isn't in the Web Store, AmaFast can't update itself. When we ship a new build the extension's popup shows an <b>Update available</b> banner pointing back here — download the new zip, unzip over the old folder, then hit the reload arrow on the extensions page.</p>

    <h2>What it will never do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Type your bank user ID, password, OTP, PIN, card number or CVV. It leaves the bank page without signing in.</li>
      <li>Solve CAPTCHAs, or retry Buy Now in the background to snipe stock.</li>
      <li>Change your quantity, variant, address or delivery option.</li>
      <li>Place an order when something other than Internet Banking is selected.</li>
      <li>Run on your bank's website.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your privacy</h2>
    <p>AmaFast has no account and no tracking. It downloads our public deals list every 20 minutes — that request carries no cookies and tells us nothing about you or what you're shopping for. When it matches a deal to a product page, the matching happens <b>on your own machine</b>, against the list already downloaded. The product you're looking at is never sent anywhere. Full detail ships in <code>PRIVACY.md</code> inside the zip.</p>

    <h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2>
    <p>Opening a deal from the AmaFast popup uses an affiliate link, and we may earn a commission on what you buy through it — at <b>no extra cost to you</b>. That's what pays for the deal hunting. AmaFast <b>never adds or changes an affiliate tag on a page you opened yourself</b>: if you found a product on your own, it only shows you the price we have on record and gets out of the way. That rule is enforced in the code, not just promised — see <code>test/invariant.sh</code> in the source.</p>

    <h2>Fine print</h2>
    <p>AmaFast is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Amazon. It automates clicks you would otherwise make yourself, on your own account, in your own browser. You are responsible for the orders you place with it — always check the order before you pay. If something goes wrong, <a href="/contact">tell us</a> and we'll fix it.</p>

    <p class="af-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary btn-lg" href="<%= release.download %>" download>⬇ Download AmaFast v<%= release.version %></a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/loot-deals">Browse today's loot deals</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
(function () {
  var btn = document.getElementById('af-copy-btn');
  if (!btn) return;
  btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
    var text = btn.getAttribute('data-copy');
    var done = function () {
      var was = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Copied ✓';
      setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = was; }, 1600);
    };
    // navigator.clipboard needs HTTPS and can be blocked; fall back to
    // selecting the text so the user can still copy it by hand.
    if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(done, select);
    } else {
      select();
    }
    function select() {
      var node = document.getElementById('af-url');
      var range = document.createRange();
      range.selectNodeContents(node);
      var sel = window.getSelection();
      sel.removeAllRanges();
      sel.addRange(range);
      try { document.execCommand('copy'); done(); } catch (e) { btn.textContent = 'Press Ctrl+C'; }
    }
  });
})();
</script>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
